## Configuration Files Specification

### `pyckage.json`
The central project configuration file. Written in standard JSON.

```json
{
  "name": "my-pyck-app",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "A premium Python application managed by PyCk",
  "author": "Developer Name <email@example.com>",
  "private": true,
  "python": "^3.13",
  "engines": {
    "python": "^3.13"
  },
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "python main.py",
    "test": "pytest"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "fastapi": "==0.136.1",
    "requests": "==2.34.2"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "pytest": "==8.0.0"
  }
}
```

### `pyckage.lock`
Autogenerated lockfile. Tracks the resolved precise pinned version of every package installed in your dependency graph. Do not modify this file manually.

